  <portType name="OneThing_x0020_API_PortType">
    <operation name="POST_signIn">
      <documentation>Signs in with an email address or a phone number, creating the account the first time. There's no password and no verification (sandbox). The response sets the `ot_session` cookie; shops created with it belong to the account and are listed on `/account`. Signing in with an email also claims older shops whose seller email matches. In a browser, sellers can instead use Log in with PayPal (`/api/account/paypal`), which also records the PayPal account their sales are paid into.</documentation>
      <input message="wsdl:POST_signIn_InputMessage" />
      <output message="wsdl:POST_signIn_OutputMessage">
        <documentation>Signed in. The `ot_session` cookie is set.</documentation>
      </output>
      <fault name="POST_signIn_400" message="wsdl:POST_signIn_400">
        <documentation>Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.</documentation>
      </fault>
    </operation>
    <operation name="POST_signOut">
      <documentation>Ends this browser's session and clears the `ot_session` cookie.</documentation>
      <input message="wsdl:POST_signOut_InputMessage" />
      <output message="wsdl:POST_signOut_OutputMessage">
        <documentation>Done.</documentation>
      </output>
    </operation>
    <operation name="GET_logInWithPayPal">
      <documentation>A link for a browser, not for code: redirects to PayPal's sign-in page. PayPal sends the seller back to `/api/account/paypal/callback`, which signs them in (creating the account the first time), records the PayPal account their sales are paid into, and redirects to `next`.</documentation>
      <input message="wsdl:GET_logInWithPayPal_InputMessage" />
      <fault name="GET_logInWithPayPal_503" message="wsdl:GET_logInWithPayPal_503">
        <documentation>Log in with PayPal isn't switched on for this server.</documentation>
      </fault>
    </operation>
    <operation name="POST_createShop">
      <documentation>Starts a draft shop from one of three sources. Gemini designs the page and guesses the
setup; check it with `getShop`, adjust with `updateShop`, then go live.

Sent with a session cookie from `signIn`, the shop belongs to that account, which also
becomes its seller email (and PayPal email, after Log in with PayPal) unless you give one.

- `source=photo`: a `photo` and/or a `description` of your own product.
- `source=link`: a `url`. If Channel3 recognises it as a store's product page, the shop
  becomes a recommendation (`product_type: referral`); otherwise the page is read and you
  sell the product yourself with PayPal.
- `source=channel3`: a `productId` from `searchProducts` (a recommendation).

Takes 15–40 seconds. Hero art, if available, is generated afterwards (`hero_status`).

**Platforms:** sent with a platform API key, the shop belongs to the key's account, so the
key can manage it from then on (no need to keep the admin token). It's made for one of the
platform's sellers, so it inherits nothing from the account: set `paypal_email` or call
`connectPayPal` for that seller.
</documentation>
      <input message="wsdl:POST_createShop_InputMessage" />
      <output message="wsdl:POST_createShop_OutputMessage">
        <documentation>Draft created.</documentation>
      </output>
      <fault name="POST_createShop_400" message="wsdl:POST_createShop_400">
        <documentation>Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.</documentation>
      </fault>
      <fault name="POST_createShop_409" message="wsdl:POST_createShop_409">
        <documentation>Taken or unavailable (a link name, or a sold-out product).</documentation>
      </fault>
      <fault name="POST_createShop_502" message="wsdl:POST_createShop_502">
        <documentation>Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.</documentation>
      </fault>
    </operation>
    <operation name="GET_getShop">
      <documentation>Everything about the shop, including the AI's design spec and guesses.</documentation>
      <input message="wsdl:GET_getShop_InputMessage" />
      <output message="wsdl:GET_getShop_OutputMessage">
        <documentation>The shop.</documentation>
      </output>
      <fault name="GET_getShop_404" message="wsdl:GET_getShop_404">
        <documentation>No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.</documentation>
      </fault>
    </operation>
    <operation name="PATCH_updateShop">
      <documentation>Changes only the fields you send. Renaming `slug` keeps the old link working (it
redirects). Set `status: live` to publish; a digital product needs its file (or, for
access codes, `access_url`) first.
</documentation>
      <input message="wsdl:PATCH_updateShop_InputMessage" />
      <output message="wsdl:PATCH_updateShop_OutputMessage">
        <documentation>Saved.</documentation>
      </output>
      <fault name="PATCH_updateShop_400" message="wsdl:PATCH_updateShop_400">
        <documentation>Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.</documentation>
      </fault>
      <fault name="PATCH_updateShop_404" message="wsdl:PATCH_updateShop_404">
        <documentation>No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.</documentation>
      </fault>
    </operation>
    <operation name="POST_refineShopDesign">
      <documentation>"Make it warmer", "shorter copy", "more premium". Gemini edits the design spec.</documentation>
      <input message="wsdl:POST_refineShopDesign_InputMessage" />
      <output message="wsdl:POST_refineShopDesign_OutputMessage">
        <documentation>The new design.</documentation>
      </output>
      <fault name="POST_refineShopDesign_400" message="wsdl:POST_refineShopDesign_400">
        <documentation>Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.</documentation>
      </fault>
      <fault name="POST_refineShopDesign_404" message="wsdl:POST_refineShopDesign_404">
        <documentation>No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.</documentation>
      </fault>
      <fault name="POST_refineShopDesign_502" message="wsdl:POST_refineShopDesign_502">
        <documentation>Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.</documentation>
      </fault>
    </operation>
    <operation name="POST_regenerateHeroArt">
      <documentation>Starts generation in the background. Poll `getShop` for `hero_status`.</documentation>
      <input message="wsdl:POST_regenerateHeroArt_InputMessage" />
      <output message="wsdl:POST_regenerateHeroArt_OutputMessage">
        <documentation>Done.</documentation>
